  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A Partnerships Platform for Settlements Outreach</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Globally, shelter responses are critically underfunded. For example, in 2021, the Global Shelter Cluster identified 47.8 million people in need of assistance, targeted only 60% of those people, and managed to assist only 17%. This was in large part due to lack of available funding. Furthermore, non-food items (NFI) were provided to only 32% of those people in need. Whilst globally, humanitarian needs remain under-resourced, the issues facing the shelter sector, with high per household costs, are particularly significant. Given the scale of needs, there is a clear need for increased efficiency and effectiveness in response driven by strong technical capacity in the field. To achieve this, there is a need to raise awareness and highlight the humanitarian shelter and settlements needs and identify new partners. 
 
The goal of this project is to Improve the shelter and settlements outcomes for crisis affected people by raising awareness on the needs for support, as well as improving expertise in humanitarian shelter, settlements and camp coordination and camp management (CCCM).</narrative>
  </description>
